---
applyTo: "**/*.{js,ts,json,md}"
description: "User experience validation for data visualizations"
---

# UX Validation Standards

## The 5-Second Test

Before generating ANY visualization, validate:
- [ ] Can the main insight be understood in 5 seconds?
- [ ] Is every visual element necessary?
- [ ] Would removing something make this clearer?
- [ ] Are we showing minimum necessary information?

## Cognitive Load Assessment

### HIGH Load (AVOID)
- 4+ overlapping time series
- Multiple legends for same dimension
- Color-only differentiation
- Dense overlapping data points

### MEDIUM Load (CAUTION)
- 3 time series with clear separation
- Single legend with 4+ items
- Mixed chart types in single view

### LOW Load (PREFERRED)
- 1-2 data series
- Clear visual hierarchy
- Direct labeling when possible
- Single focused insight

## Multi-Series Decision Tree

### When user requests 4+ data series:

1. **Check patterns**: Similar trends? → Small multiples
2. **Check importance**: One primary? → Highlight primary, gray others  
3. **Check task**: Comparing values? → Horizontal bar chart
4. **Check temporal**: Trends essential? → Limit to 3 most important

### Implementation Templates

#### Small Multiples (Preferred)
```json
{
  "facet": {
    "field": "category",
    "type": "nominal", 
    "columns": 2
  },
  "spec": {
    "mark": {"type": "line", "color": "#4477AA"},
    "encoding": {
      "x": {"field": "date", "type": "temporal"},
      "y": {"field": "value", "type": "quantitative"}
    }
  }
}
```

#### Highlight + Context
```json
{
  "layer": [
    {
      "mark": {"type": "line", "color": "#CCCCCC", "strokeWidth": 1},
      "encoding": {
        "detail": {"field": "series", "type": "nominal"},
        "x": {"field": "date", "type": "temporal"},
        "y": {"field": "value", "type": "quantitative"}
      }
    },
    {
      "mark": {"type": "line", "color": "#4477AA", "strokeWidth": 3},
      "transform": [{"filter": "datum.series == 'Primary'"}],
      "encoding": {
        "x": {"field": "date", "type": "temporal"},
        "y": {"field": "value", "type": "quantitative"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Legend Validation

### The One Legend Rule
- Count total legends in specification
- If > 1, consolidate or remove redundant ones
- Priority: Color > Pattern > Shape > Size

### Auto-Fix Function
```javascript
function consolidateLegends(spec) {
  const legendFields = [];
  
  if (spec.encoding.color?.legend !== null) legendFields.push('color');
  if (spec.encoding.shape?.legend !== null) legendFields.push('shape');
  if (spec.encoding.strokeDash?.legend !== null) legendFields.push('strokeDash');
  
  // Keep only the highest priority legend
  if (legendFields.length > 1) {
    if (legendFields.includes('color')) {
      spec.encoding.shape = {...spec.encoding.shape, legend: null};
      spec.encoding.strokeDash = {...spec.encoding.strokeDash, legend: null};
    } else if (legendFields.includes('shape')) {
      spec.encoding.strokeDash = {...spec.encoding.strokeDash, legend: null};
    }
  }
  
  return spec;
}
```

## Visual Hierarchy Rules

### Title Strategy
- Sentence case only (not Title Case)
- Action-oriented when possible
- Include key insight in title

### Color Strategy  
- Maximum 4 colors in single chart
- Use color to emphasize, not just categorize
- Gray for context/secondary information

### Layout Strategy
- Left-align titles and labels
- Horizontal legends when space allows
- Remove chart borders and gridlines (reduce noise)